# Normalize text files to LF in the index and in the working tree on every
# platform.
#
# Without this, a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true -- what the Git for
# Windows installer configures by default -- rewrites tracked files to CRLF.
# That silently breaks anything comparing generated output byte-for-byte against
# a checked-in fixture: pkg/configuration's tests hash testdata/*.yaml against
# the config the CLI writes, and the CLI always writes LF.
#
# "text=auto" still detects binary content and leaves it untouched.
* text=auto eol=lf
